[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-12564"] :question/problem "$\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+3)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-349217/field-1/4bf78ee97047b11e3f0b99df1d2ac8693ecb270ef81d2b88779d50c1336da4f9" :answer/id #uuid "b921defa-1211-5826-a8e9-e8b187eee7f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}e^4+\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349217/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f50aba1-c314-5a83-8359-d16e3fe2c6a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349217/field-1/4bf78ee97047b11e3f0b99df1d2ac8693ecb270ef81d2b88779d50c1336da4f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-349217/field-1/4bf78ee97047b11e3f0b99df1d2ac8693ecb270ef81d2b88779d50c1336da4f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349217" :question/id #uuid "24fe0b51-6352-5f7d-ac11-80fbb39fffe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-349217" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}3x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(2\\cdot {e}^{4}-0\\cdot {e}^{0})-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{4}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9{e}^{4}+3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349217/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
